</ul>

Q: Make Playwright MS Edge screenshots stable and platform independent A: <p>Why this happens in Edge 140+:</p>
<p>Recently Edge and Chrome updated their headless engine. Unlike the old Headless mode which was a separate browser implementation, the new headless is nearly identical to the &quot;Headed&quot; browser, meaning it more aggressively pulls from the host OS font rendering subsystem like FreeType and FontConfig and GPU-accelerated text functions.</p>
<p>Solution:</p>
<p>To fix this, strip all machine-varying &quot;beautification&quot; features. Try adding these launchOptions to your playwright.config.ts:</p>
<pre><code>{
  browserName: 'chromium',
  channel: 'msedge',
  launchOptions: {
    args: [

      '--font-render-hinting=none',
      '--disable-font-subpixel-positioning',
      '--disable-lcd-text',

      //  disable OS specific features
      '--disable-gpu',
      '--force-color-profile=srgb',
      '--disable-field-trial-config',
      '--disable-variations',

      // new for Chromium 140+
      '--disable-skia-runtime-opts', // Ensures Skia (graphics engine) uses generic paths
    ],
  },
}
</code></pre>
<p>As a fallback if the pixels still differ, switch to SSIM (Structural similarity index) which ignores too tiny to see microscopic subpixel shifts:</p>
<pre><code>await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot({
  _comparator: 'ssim-cie94', //supported in recent versions of Playwright
  threshold: 0.2,
});
</code></pre>

Q: Project raised exception class &#39;External: SIGFPE&#39; A: <h2><strong>Fix for SIGFPE crash on TImage click:</strong></h2>
<p>The crash happened because the FPU floating point unit, was in a “bad state” before opening the dialog GTK and TImage code can trigger a SIGFPE if floating point exceptions are unmasked.</p>
<p>I fixed it by Resting the FPU exception mask before showing the dialog, resetting the mask clears that state. Finally!</p>
<pre><code>uses Math;

procedure ResetFPU;
begin
  SetExceptionMask([exInvalidOp, exDenormalized, exZeroDivide,
                    exOverflow, exUnderflow, exPrecision]);
end;

procedure TpmAlbum.imgAlbumCoverClick(Sender: TObject);
begin
